35,2,1,talk,May,,"Wow, the news isn't great! The truck arrives as early as 7:40 AM, which is way too early for some of us. Plus, the paperwork for a permanent build is a total nightmare—five signatures and four months? No thanks!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The data confirms my suspicions. The burden is not shared; one household has filed nearly all the complaints. It is clear that the current location is an unfair source of stress for one neighbor.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found some big numbers! We're spending 34,000 yen every year just on nets and deodorants because of the open bags. Also, new shelters are really expensive—around 248,000 yen on average, even with the ward's help!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That sounds like a lot of money, Kenji. I found that the station block's bin house actually smells quite sour in the summer because you can't wash the floor. We should be very careful about choosing a structure.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My research reveals a physical disparity in our frontages; some of us have ample space, while others have very little. Furthermore, the station block's history shows that structures often lead to disputes over maintenance. We must be mindful.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, if one person is doing all the complaining, it's probably because they're the one stuck with the bins at their gate! We can't just call a plan ""equal"" if it keeps things exactly as they are.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, exactly. The data shows a clear imbalance of burden. However, we must also be realistic; the residents' meeting statements show that no one is willing to act as a ""trash police"" for their neighbors. We need a solution that doesn't rely on policing.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, that's a tough problem! But if we spend 34,000 yen every year just on smells and nets, maybe we can use that money to find a better way? I'm worried that a big expensive shelter might be too much for some of us!","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, I agree. A very expensive shelter might cause more stress than it solves. I also worry that if we build something that smells like the station block's house, it might only make our neighbors more unhappy with each other.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is wise to consider both the cost and the scent, for a burden on the wallet or the nose can weigh heavily on the heart. We must seek a path that is light for everyone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Servas, you're always so dreamy, but we need to be practical! If we just pick the ""lightest"" path, we might just be leaving the same person to suffer. We need a plan that actually moves the burden!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, you are right. Moving the burden is necessary, but we must ensure we don't simply shift the annoyance to another household. A solution that requires strict supervision will likely fail given the residents' reluctance.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, @May, I agree! We have to move the bins so it's fair, but we can't forget the money. If we pick something too expensive, some of our neighbors might really struggle to pay for it!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, you're right to be concerned about the cost. I also wonder if a rotating system, like the supervised mornings I saw on the next lane, might be a gentler way to share the work without spending too much.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, a rotating system is a gentle thought. However, we must ask ourselves: who will manage the schedule? I have seen many agreements crumble when the labor quietly falls upon the one who answers the phone first.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"@Servas, you hit the nail on the head! That's exactly what I'm afraid of. If we aren't careful, ""sharing"" just becomes a fancy word for letting one person do all the work again. We need a real change!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Servas, your point about the management of a schedule is valid. If we implement a rotation, it must be a system that is self-sustaining and doesn't create a new administrative burden for one person. We need a structural change, not just a shift in chores.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! We need a real change that doesn't just move the work around. But we have to be careful—if we build something big, the cost could be huge! Let's find a way that's fair and affordable for everyone!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. I just hope that whatever we decide, it's something that helps us all get along again. I'd hate for a new system to create more tension between us as neighbors.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us remember that the most enduring solutions are those that respect the time and energy of every soul. A plan is only as fair as the effort it demands from the quietest among us.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
