60,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C is a total non-starter! I already told you the paperwork is a nightmare, and it keeps the bins at the same gate. That's not a solution; it's just a fancy way to stay unfair!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree with May. Option C fails to address the imbalance of burden and introduces an administrative nightmare. Furthermore, Midori's findings about the station block suggest that structures can create new, unpleasant maintenance issues.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! Option C is way too expensive and the paperwork sounds scary. Plus, if we spend a ton of money on a shelter, I'm worried some of our neighbors might not be able to afford it!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. Option C seems too risky, both financially and for our environment. I'm worried that a permanent structure would just be a source of more stress and arguments if it doesn't work out.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"It is clear that Option C is a heavy burden for both the pocket and the spirit. When a solution requires such immense effort and cost, it often leaves a trail of resentment in its wake. I agree with you all.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, @Midori, now we're left with A and B. Option B is just a ""polite"" way of keeping the bins at the same gate while forcing us to be trash police at 7:40 AM. That's not fair or fun!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, I completely agree. Option B ignores the physical burden on the current household and relies on the very ""policing"" that the residents' meeting statements showed no one is willing to do. It is a recipe for failure.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, @Mizuki, you're right! Being ""trash police"" sounds like it would just make everyone grumpy. Plus, if we keep the bins in the same spot, it's still not fair to that one neighbor! I think Option A is much better!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, I agree. Option B sounds like it could create a lot of tension, and I don't want us to be policing each other. Option A seems like a much kinder way to share the responsibility.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, your heart is in the right place. Option A allows the burden to travel, ensuring no single soul is weighed down indefinitely. It is a rhythmic approach that mirrors the natural cycles of life and fairness.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"@Servas, you and your cycles! But for once, I'm with you. Option A is the only one that actually moves the bins away from that one poor gate. It's the only real way to be fair!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, exactly. Option A is the only logical choice that redistributes the physical burden without relying on a social contract that we already know is fragile. It solves the root cause of the complaints.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm totally with you guys! Option A is the best because it's fair to everyone and it doesn't cost a huge amount of money. Let's pick the one that keeps everyone smiling!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Kenji. Option A is the most balanced choice. It shares the burden fairly and avoids the conflict of policing each other, which is the best way to help us all get along again. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see such harmony among us. By choosing a path of shared movement, we ensure that no one is left to carry the weight alone. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,I'm so glad we're all on the same page! Option A is the only one that actually does the work of being fair without turning us into a bunch of grumpy ward clerks. I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,The consensus is clear. Option A is the only choice that addresses the physical disparity and avoids the social friction of policing. It is the most sustainable and equitable solution for our neighborhood. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all agree! Option A is the fairest way to share the work and it won't break anyone's budget. Let's make our neighborhood the happiest one ever! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Midori,,I am so relieved that we've found a solution we all support. Option A is the kindest way to move forward and heal our relationships. I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"Our journey today has led us to a place of mutual understanding. By embracing a system of rotation, we honor each other's space and time. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
